Runtime: Context Manifest

Purpose:
  Define the context manifest template and usage for debugging AI decisions.
  Context manifest records what knowledge was loaded, excluded, missed, and
  the confidence rating for each task execution, enabling explainability
  and debugging of AI context decisions.

Principles:
  Context manifest is created for every task execution.
  Manifest is immutable once created.
  Manifest enables debugging of incorrect AI decisions.
  Manifest is versioned with execution for reproducibility.
  Manifest is never used as knowledge source; it is audit artifact only.

ManifestTemplate:
  task: task_id
  execution_id: execution_id
  timestamp: ISO8601

  loaded:
    - reference: canonical reference id
      relevance: direct | indirect | historical | optional
      trust: explicit_constraint | decision | validated_skill | established | best_practice | ai_suggestion
      importance: critical | high | normal | low | temporary
      source: file_path or knowledge_store
      loaded_by: auto | always_load | human_override | escalation
      rationale: why this reference was loaded

  excluded:
    - reference: canonical reference id
      reason: irrelevant | excluded_by_policy | budget_overflow | stale | deprecated | excluded_by_human
      excluded_by: auto | human_override | budget
      rationale: why this reference was excluded

  missed:
    - reference: canonical reference id or keyword
      reason: not_found | unresolved_dependency | access_denied | not_available
      impact: implementation_blocker | partial | minor
      action: expand_context | human_escalation | defer

  context_confidence:
    level: insufficient | partial | sufficient | high
    score: integer (0-100)
    criteria_met:
      - all_required_references_loaded: boolean
      - all_dependencies_resolved: boolean
      - all_constraints_identified: boolean
      - negative_knowledge_checked: boolean
      - decisions_reviewed: boolean
      - skills_verified: boolean
    rationale: explanation of confidence level

  overrides:
    - type: @context.include | @context.exclude
      reference: canonical reference id
      rationale: human-provided reason
      authority: human_id or role

  trust_conflicts:
    - reference_a: reference id
      reference_b: reference id
      conflict: description
      resolution: higher_trust_wins | human_decision
      rationale: explanation

  escalation:
    - trigger: insufficient_context | knowledge_gap | ambiguity | conflict
      action: expand_context | request_human | defer_task
      result: resolved | pending | escalated

  budget:
    allocated_tokens: integer
    used_tokens: integer
    allocated_refs: integer
    used_refs: integer
    overflow_handling: trim_low | trim_optional | trim_historical | request_more

ManifestUsage:
  debugging:
    scenario: AI made incorrect decision
    action: inspect manifest loaded and missed sections
    example:
      developer: "AI why did it choose Kafka?"
      manifest:
        loaded:
          - @generic.messaging.kafka
        missed:
          - @project.messaging.rabbitmq
      diagnosis: context retrieval was incorrect

  explainability:
    scenario: AI decision trace
    action: generate decision trace from manifest
    example:
      input: async notification
      loaded: @messaging, @project.payment, @decision.rabbitmq
      rejected: Kafka
      reason: project decision explicitly prefers RabbitMQ

  auditing:
    scenario: compliance or security review
    action: verify context included required constraints
    example:
      check: @constitution.security in loaded?
      check: @constitution.data-integrity in loaded?

  optimization:
    scenario: improve context retrieval accuracy
    action: analyze missed references to improve ranking
    example:
      missed: @project.payment.rabbitmq
      action: adjust ranking weight for project-scoped decisions

ManifestLifecycle:
  created: at task start, before context loading
  finalized: at task completion, after consolidation
  stored: with execution record
  retained: for debugging and auditing
  rule: manifest is immutable after finalization
  rule: manifest is never used as knowledge source

Navigation:
  Runtime: @INDEX.sdd
  Memory Model: @memory-model.sdd
  Context Builder: @context-builder.sdd
  Context Policy: @context-policy.sdd
  Memory Consolidation: @memory-consolidation.sdd
  Execution: @execution.sdd
  Knowledge: @../knowledge/INDEX.sdd

Rules:
  [RT-CTX-MAN-01] Context manifest is created for every task execution.
  [RT-CTX-MAN-02] Manifest is immutable once finalized.
  [RT-CTX-MAN-03] Manifest is never used as knowledge source; it is an audit artifact only.
  [RT-CTX-MAN-04] Manifest records loaded, excluded, missed, confidence, overrides, and trust conflicts.
  [RT-CTX-MAN-05] Manifest is versioned with execution for reproducibility.
  [RT-CTX-MAN-06] Human overrides are logged with task ID and rationale.
  [RT-CTX-MAN-07] Missed references include impact assessment and required action.
  [RT-CTX-MAN-08] Trust conflicts are recorded with resolution and rationale.
  [RT-CTX-MAN-09] Manifest enables debugging of incorrect AI context decisions.
  [RT-CTX-MAN-10] Manifest enables explainability of AI decisions on demand.
  [RT-CTX-MAN-11] Manifest retention period matches execution record retention.
  [RT-CTX-MAN-12] Agent MUST NOT add signatures or sign-offs to manifest outputs.
  [RT-CTX-MAN-13] Agent MUST NOT use emojis, icons, or decorative symbols in manifest output headers or titles.

State: +
